Replace rusty-cogs' `include()` of the Clockwork override segment with the
bazel_dep declarations its own packages need.

Bazel accepts `include()` only in the root module, and rusty-cogs is a
dependency here, so its MODULE.bazel cannot be evaluated as written --
resolution fails before any target is analyzed. The segment it includes is the
Clockwork drop's dependency table: versionless `bazel_dep`s plus the overrides
that satisfy them. This repo carries its own verbatim copy of that table and
includes it from the root, where the directive is legal and where the overrides
are the ones Bazel honours, so the only thing rusty-cogs still needs from it is
*visibility*: a module can name `@clockwork` only if it declares a dep on it.
The list below is exactly the table entries rusty-cogs' own `.bzl` and
`BUILD.bazel` files reference by repo name; every one is versionless because the
root's overrides pin it.

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
index ac85550..511e2dc 100644
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -7,7 +7,16 @@
 
 module(name = "rusty_cogs")
 
-include("//bazel:clockwork_overrides.MODULE.bazel")
+bazel_dep(name = "bazel_skylib")
+bazel_dep(name = "build_stack_rules_proto")
+bazel_dep(name = "clockwork")
+bazel_dep(name = "platforms")
+bazel_dep(name = "rules_cc")
+bazel_dep(name = "rules_proto")
+bazel_dep(name = "rules_python")
+bazel_dep(name = "rules_shell")
+bazel_dep(name = "xxhash")
+bazel_dep(name = "zstd")
 
 # The interpreter the drop pins for its own Python code and both of its pip
 # hubs. Those hubs are version-keyed, and the Clockwork compiler's dependency
